-- Eight contacts on a threat board, two of them friendly. The pipeline reads left to right — filter, order, take — and the result is a selection like any other: it can stand bare as a query or take an effect.
-- Grade indices live in the filtered index space and are mapped through /enemy before touching world rows:
-- the two non-enemies carry the highest raw threat (95, 99) and must never be picked.
--! registry ../registries/042-pipeline-topk.reg
--! out 6 3 4 0 7
--! expect targeted = 1 1 0 1 1 0 1 1

Enemy |> order by Threat desc |> take 5
Enemy |> order by Threat desc |> take 5 , +Targeted
